claims:
1. A method for authenticating a video stream by:
Quantizing the stream into time segments of pre-deter-mined size to create Quantized Clips;
Determining a summary measure of each of said Quantized Clips;
Attaching a time stamp and geo-location stamp to each of the Quantized Clips;
At the end time of each Quantized Clip, minting an NFT for each of the Quantized Clips by registering on the blockchain assigned to the wallet of the source thereby registering the time of capture of the Quantized Clips.

3. A Method as in claim 1, wherein in trade with users:
Recognizing that each user may require a unique subset of the collection of Quantized Clips;
Trading a set of said Quantized Clips of the video stream to accommodate said subset of said Quantized Clips made available to users trading their respective NFTs; thereby, trading the resulting NFTs.

4. A method for authenticating a plurality of concurrent video streams, each as in claim 1, wherein said plurality of video streams comprise a ensemble of video streams by:
Quantizing with common time slots, the elements of the ensemble of streams into time segments of pre-deter-mined size to create Ensemble Sets of Quantized Clips;
Determining a summary measure of each of said Ensemble Sets of Quantized Clips;
Attaching a time stamp and geo-location stamp to each of the Ensemble Sets of Quantized Clips;
At the end time of each Ensemble Set of Quantized Clip, minting an NFT for each of the Quantized Clips by registering on the blockchain assigned to the wallet of the source thereby registering the time of capture of each of the Ensemble Set of Quantized Clips.

5. A method for crowd sourced protection by trusted protectors in a community by:
Creating a social network with members of the commu-nity as members of the network;
Defining trust circles for each of the members of the network;
Constructing directional trust chain linkages from trusted member to beneficiary of the trust;
In the event of a need for protection for a threatened member of the community;
Enabling the threatened member to alert the network on a device interface wherein said device has a camera to record and stream voice and or video;
Building a first element of one or more trust chains from the threatened member as the beneficiary of trust to the first level trusted members;
Building a second element of each of said trust chains from the first level trust member to one or more second level trust members as trusted members;
Upon request from the threatened member, invoking signaling to one or more levels of trust members to construct a response team, to address the threat; thereby relieving the threat.
